# Proof Record — Fort Lauderdale Real Estate Office

category: "applied-ontology-methods"
updated: "2025"

## Context

A commercial real estate office in Fort Lauderdale, Florida. The office was operating at a modest revenue level with no clear path to significant growth. Gene Berman, who wrote the foreword to the Advisory Selling Method™, was associated with this engagement.

## Starting Constraint

The office was performing below its potential. Standard sales training and management approaches had not produced breakthrough results. The ceiling was structural, not tactical.

## Applied Ontology Methods™ Application

The Advisory Selling Method™ — the Applied Ontological Method extended into the domain of selling and client relationships. Inceptive, not Deceptive. Eductive, not Aggressive.

## Implementation Summary

The Advisory Selling Method™ was implemented across the office over a sustained period. The method transformed how advisors conducted selling conversations — from adversarial and agenda-based to commitment-based and collaborative.

## Outcome

Revenue grew from $2 million to $37 million over six years.

